# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment variables
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and fill in. `.env.local` is only read in
# development; on Vercel set the same keys in Project Settings → Environment.
#
# Nothing here is required for the site to build or run. The contact form is the
# only feature that needs a value, and until it is set the form says so plainly
# instead of pretending a message was sent.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# --- Contact form (required for the form to actually deliver) ---------------
# Where a validated contact submission is POSTed as JSON:
#   { name, email, phone?, message, submittedAt, source }
#
# Works with any HTTPS endpoint that accepts a JSON POST — a form backend
# (Formspree, Basin, Getform, …), an email relay, a Zapier/Make hook, or your
# own handler.
#
# Leaving this unset is a supported state, not a broken one: `POST /api/contact`
# responds 503 with `code: "not_configured"`, and the form tells the visitor to
# email or call instead. Do NOT set it to a placeholder — a fake URL will make
# the form report failures on every submission.
#
# Treat the value as a secret: webhook URLs usually carry a token in the path
# or query string. It is read server-side only and is never logged or returned
# to the browser.
# CONTACT_WEBHOOK_URL=https://example.com/your-endpoint


# --- Site URL (strongly recommended) ----------------------------------------
# The site's public origin. Drives metadataBase, every canonical URL, the
# sitemap and robots.txt, so it must be the real deployed origin — a wrong value
# produces wrong absolute URLs across the whole site.
#
# Defaults to "https://example.com" when unset, which is correct for local work
# but wrong in production. Set it.
#
# `NEXT_PUBLIC_` is required: it is inlined at build time, so the value stays
# safe to read from client components and is not a secret.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-domain.com


# --- Analytics: none configured --------------------------------------------
# No analytics, tracking pixel, chat widget or marketing tag ships with this
# template, and no identifier from the site it was cloned from was carried over.
# The only scripts it loads at runtime are its own; the OG image is rendered at
# build time and pulls in nothing.
#
# If you add analytics, configure it for YOUR business and add consent handling
# to match — the cookie notice in the footer is built for exactly this.


# --- Notes for self-hosted / standalone deployments -------------------------
# This project builds with `output: "standalone"`, so the production server is
# `.next/standalone/server.js` (after copying `.next/static` and `public/` into
# it). `next.config.ts` security headers ARE applied by that server — this was
# verified by `scripts/qa-headers.mjs`, not assumed.
#
# If you add a third-party script (analytics, a booking embed, a chat widget),
# revisit the Content-Security-Policy note in next.config.ts and
# TEMPLATE_GUIDE.md before enabling one.
